sblg is a utility for creating static blogs. It merges articles into templates
to generate static HTML files, Atom feeds, and JSON files. It's built for use
with make(1). No PHP, no database: just a simple UNIX tool for pulling data from
articles and populating templates.

How does it work? You write your HTML (really XHTML) articles and templates.
sblg(1) pulls data from the articles and merges it into the templates. This is
usually orchestrated with a Makefile. And that's it. You can write articles in
any format — like Markdown — so long it converts into XHTML.
